---
/**
 * StackLinks — the "stack" entry strip on product pages.
 *
 * A compact card under the products hero (catalog + product detail) that
 * hands buyers two destinations: the stack itself (the /features/ document
 * that breaks the AHA stack down) and the services offering (/services/).
 * Mirrors the Django pages/partials/stack_links.html include (same copy, so
 * both render roads carry the same entry point).
 */
---

<section class="container-fusion" style="padding-top:1.5rem;">
  <div class="card flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-5 p-6">
    <div class="max-w-xl">
      <p class="tag-marker mb-2">stack</p>
      <p class="m-0 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-fu-text/80">
        Every product ships on the AHA stack — server-rendered HTML, HTMX
        fragments, Alpine micro-interactions — with Wagtail content and
        allauth auth behind it. Or bring us in to build yours.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <a href="/features/" class="btn-primary !px-5 !py-2.5 text-sm">
        The stack
        <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"/>
        </svg>
      </a>
      <a href="/services/" class="btn-secondary !px-5 !py-2.5 text-sm">Services →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
